+The supervisor imports no torch.
+- **Per arm.** It writes the start record (both ledger roots) and only then spawns the child.
+- **Limits.** On one ``time.monotonic()`` clock, it enforces:
+  - the arm limit, from that arm's start record;
+  - the aggregate limit, from the invocation record, shared by all arms;
+  - the RSS cap, sampled every ``poll_interval_s``.
+- **Stops.** A soft stop is given to the child. At the hard deadline, or when the RSS cap is exceeded, the child is
+  killed.
+- **After an ordinary outcome.** COMPLETED_PASS or COMPLETED_FIT_FAIL under the primary policy, and EXECUTION_ERROR
+  of one arm, are recorded, and the next registered arm runs.
+- **Global stops,** which end the invocation:
+  - a guard kill (RSS or deadline) or an INCOMPLETE arm;
+  - an interrupt;
+  - an exhausted aggregate budget.
+  The remaining arms are recorded as NOT_RUN, with the reason.
+- **Degenerate tile.** It gets no start and no child: it is recorded NOT_RUN with reason ``degenerate registered
+  input``. The primary policy classifies it DEGENERATE_INPUT, class F.
+- **Abrupt supervisor death.** A start record without an end record marks the arm INCOMPLETE, and every later
+  invocation is refused.
 """
 
